<h2>The Vault System — Main Vault and Wiki Vault</h2>
<p>Obsidian is fundamentally built on the <strong>vault</strong> system. A vault is a <strong>collection of markdown files</strong> bundled under a single name, and it is read as one set. It is the same structure as Claude Code opening a particular folder, reading the <code>CLAUDE.md</code> inside it, and taking on a distinct identity.</p>

<h3>Separate knowledge written by AI from knowledge written by you</h3>
<p>Wherever possible, it is best to <strong>separate knowledge written by AI from knowledge written by you into different vaults</strong>. It is easy to mistake what AI produced for something you fully understand yourself, so it matters to <strong>draw a strict line</strong> around how far your own study has actually gone.</p>

